quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  7,144,He said: ‘O Musa (Moses)! I have chosen you above (all other) people with My messages and My speech. So take hold of what I have given you and be among the grateful.’
  7,145,"And We inscribed for him on the Tablets (of the Torah) admonition, and an exposition of all (necessary) things. (And We said:) ‘Hold on to them firmly and command your people to take the best of (what is in) them. I will soon show you the abode of the transgressors."
  7,146,"I will turn away from My revelations those who act arrogantly on the earth without justice. Even if they were to see every sign, they would not believe in it. And if they were to see the path of guidance, they still would not adopt it as (their) path. And if they were to see the way of error, they would adopt it as (their) way. That is because they rejected Our revelations and remained negligent of them.’"
  7,147,"And those who deny Our revelations and the meeting of the Hereafter, their deeds have come to nothing. Should they be rewarded except for what they used to do?"
  7,148,"And while he was away, the people of Musa (Moses) took up (for worship) a calf (made) from their ornaments—a mere body that made sounds like a cow. Did they not see that it could neither speak to them nor guide them to the (right) path? Yet they took it up (for worship). And they were wrongdoers."
  7,149,"And when they felt ashamed of what they had done and realised that they had really gone astray, they said: ‘If our Lord does not have mercy upon us and forgive us, we shall surely be among the losers.’"
